hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24156","Ismail narrated to us, from Uthman al-Batti, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Salamah, from his father, from his grandfather, that his parents disputed over him to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one of them Muslim and the other disbeliever. He gave him choice, and he turned to the disbeliever of them. He said: O Allah, guide him. He turned to the Muslim, and he judged for him with him."
"24157","Hushaym narrated to us, Uthman Abu Amr al-Batti narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Salamah, that his grandfather accepted Islam in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his grandmother did not accept Islam, and he had from her a son. They disputed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: If you wish, you give the boy choice. He said: He seated the father in a side and the mother in a side, gave him choice, and he went toward his mother. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, guide him. He said: He returned to his father."
"24158","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, my father told me, from my grandfather Rafi ibn Sinan, that he accepted Islam and his wife refused to accept Islam. She came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: My daughter, while she is weaned or similar, and Rafi said: My daughter. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Sit in a side, and said to her: Sit in a side. He seated the little girl between them, then said: Call her. She leaned to her mother. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, guide her. She leaned to her father, and he took her."
"24159","Ismail narrated to us, Uthman al-Batti informed us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Salamah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the pecking of the crow, and the spreading of the beast of prey, and that a man fix his place in prayer as the camel fixes."
"24160","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Uthman al-Batti, from Abd al-Hamid al-Ansari, from his father, from his grandfather, that his grandfather accepted Islam and his wife refused to accept Islam. He came with a small son of his who had not reached. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seated the father here and the mother here, then gave him choice and said: O Allah, guide him. He went to his father."
